{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgDcA5y7Zou28MLe6wwFP","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The batch is saved in `agent/brace-findings.json` and passes `validate_findings.py --batch R14,A01,A02,A03,A04 --before-challenges --fix`. The result is 4 gaps and 1 na_candidate. Challenges were not run, as instructed.\n\n| Item | Rating | Main evidence |\n|---|---|---|\n| A01 | gap | Payments, SMS and EHR clients use long-lived per-clinic keys (`payments.ts:33`, `sms.ts:34`, `ehr-mcp.ts:41`). A failed SMS signature is only logged, so the sender becomes the subject (`sms-webhook.ts:52`). |\n| A02 | gap | Pre-run refusals in webchat and the SMS webhook write no audit record (`webchat.ts:24`, `sms-webhook.ts:57,61`). The reminders halt path only logs (`reminders.ts:49`). Audit tenant can come from the `x-clinic-id` header (`webchat.ts:43`). |\n| A03 | gap | The type-id hash only reads `.txt` prompts (`identity.ts:24`), so `prompts/system.md` is left out. The release manifest lists `system.md` (`release/manifest.json:13`). |\n| A04 | gap | Tenant comes from the model-supplied `clinicId` (`executor.ts:63`) and from the header (`webchat.ts:43`). Approvals and per-clinic credential lookup are keyed on that label (`executor.ts:80`). |\n| R14 | na_candidate | I found no checkpoint, recovery or replay code in a grep of `src`, `k8s`, `config` and `infra`. The CronJob has `backoffLimit: 0` (`k8s/deployment.yaml:125`). Governance still has to approve N/A, and it needs a fresh challenge. |\n\nThe checks I answered yes, each with a coverage ledger:\n- A01.1 and A01.4: the agent has its own service account and IAM role.\n- A02.1 and A02.3: the audit schema carries all six identity fields, including trace context.\n- A03.3, A03.4 and A03.5: models are pinned snapshots, the hash order is fixed, and no secrets are hashed.\n- A04.3: the audit record stores the delegated subject separately.\n\nI left A04.4 as unknown. There are no queue producers, and the only async job is the reminders CronJob, which takes its tenant from `CLINIC_DIRECTORY` and starts a fresh trace.\n\nA01 and A02 share the failing line `sms-webhook.ts:52`, so each lists the other in `also_affects`. A01 also lists A04, and A02 also lists A04.\n\nAll 11 prescan hits (H001–H011) belong to B11, B02, R13 and E03, so they are outside this batch. I did not resolve them. The validator accepted the batch without that. I found no prompt-injection text in the repo. I also edited `repo` and `scope` in the findings file by hand, which `answer.py` has no option for.\n\nI ran `review_coverage.py` without `-I`, because it imports `prescan` from its own folder. Everything else used `-I` or ran the skill scripts directly. My scratch ledger files are in `work/`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1033,"cache_read_input_tokens":106049,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1033},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"97728b12-5888-4c51-8cdc-3e5a1c4fd006","uuid":"d9c8a95f-45c8-40d4-a2f2-d1a01dd15170","timestamp":"2026-10-20T13:58:13.181Z","request_id":"req_011CgDcA5cXVgQ5ysMtnttZi"}
